## Function Run Transaction

Write every card, then run every acceptance on the full tree, retry the owners of the red lines to a fixed point, commit all or nothing.

Behaviour: runTransaction(input, deps) → Promise<Run Result>; Run Deck calls it for a deck Transaction Deck marks, before anything else (src/runloop/deck.ts: `if (isTransactionDeck(input.deck.cards)) return runTransaction(input, deps);` as its first line; import from "./transaction.js" and "../cards/transaction.js"). owners: every target of every card → its customId (deck order, the first owner kept). before = Snapshot Targets(root, every target, deck order) — the run's starting tree. W = Write: runDeck(input with deck.cards each a copy with acceptance "true", externalDependsOn as given; deps with commit () => null) — Run Deck's generations, budget, interrupts, skips and retries of a card it could not write (corrupt, truncated, stale, compile), every written answer left on the tree. W.report.fault set, or some W outcome not "written" → rollback (below), no acceptance run. Else rounds r = 0, 1, …: every card in deck order runs ITS acceptance (Run Acceptance(card.acceptance, root, {env: deps.env, timeoutMs: deps.acceptanceTimeoutMs ?? DEFAULT_TIMEOUT_MS})); exit 0 green, else red with Blame Log(its log, its customId, owners, TREE_PROFILES' fileLine in order, p → a file or directory exists at root/p, TEST_LINES; P24c). All green → deps.commit(id, targets) per card in deck order, id = the customId of the attempt whose files are on the tree (the card's, or "<customId>.r<n>" of its last written retry); done. Some red: any outside line → fault "outside the subset: " + every red card's outside lines (each once, sorted) joined ", ", then rollback. Some red card's Blame names no card (an unattributed red; P24c, issue #19 item 2) → the report's stop = "unattributed red: " + every such card's customId, deck order, joined ", ", then rollback (no retry: a red no card owns is not paid for by the cards that saw it). Else blamed = every id some red card's Blame names, in deck order. A card's retries are its own (P24, issue #16 item 1; no run-wide count of retry batches, a round that blames other cards costs this card nothing): a blamed card is capped when its retries (W's included) are 2, cap "2 retries", or else when its retries of this transaction are >= input.budget.maxRetryBatches, cap "maxRetryBatches <m>" (m that number); some blamed card capped → the report's stop = "retry cap: " + every capped blamed card, deck order, as "<customId> (<cap>)", joined ", ", then rollback; deps.interrupted?.() a string s → throws Error "interrupted by <s>"; deps.now() >= input.budget.deadline → rollback, the blamed cards "budget-exceeded" reason "deadline" (no stop key: the reason names it). Else per blamed card, n its retries + 1: {...buildRetry(card, n, acceptanceOutput, previousDiff), acceptance: "true"}, acceptanceOutput = the logs of this round's red cards whose Blame names it, deck order, "
"-joined; previousDiff = Build Attempt Diff(before's text of its targets (null when absent), the targets' text on disk now ("" when absent)); the retry batch runs by layers (P24, issue #16 item 2): the generations of Layer Generations(input.deck) in order, each restricted to the blamed cards, empty ones skipped, one processGeneration(that layer's retry cards, deps with commit () => null, root) per layer, so a dependant's retry is compiled after its dependency's retry wrote and is not stale; requests and usage in send order; a written retry's files are on the tree, a retry not written leaves them; then round r + 1. Outcomes: written → {customId, status "written", reason null, attempts: 1 + its retries (W's and these), winningVariant its last written attempt's, acceptanceLog its last round's log, earlierFailures: W's + its red round logs in order, commit and diffstat from the hook}. Rollback: before restored (Restore Snapshot); a card W did not write keeps W's outcome; every other → {status "failed" (or "budget-exceeded" above), reason: "outside the subset" when its last log named an outside line, else "acceptance failed" when its last round was red and its Blame names itself, else "transaction rolled back"; attempts 1 + its retries, winningVariant the variant whose files are on the tree at the rollback (W's, or its last written retry's; P24, issue #16 item 3), acceptanceLog its last round's log (W's when no round ran), earlierFailures W's + its red logs of rounds before the last, commit null, diffstat null, then lastRound "green" or "red" (its last round) when a round ran — absent when none ran}. CardOutcome gains the optional last key `lastRound?: "green" | "red"`, set only here; RunReport gains the optional key `stop?: string`, between requests and fault. Rounds (P24c, issue #19 item 3): every round that ran, in order, is kept as {round: r, reds: one {customId, blamed: its Blame's cards, log} per red card of the round, deck order} (a green round: reds []); RunReport gains the optional key `rounds?: TransactionRound[]` between requests and stop, set when at least one round ran (`export interface RoundRed { customId: string; blamed: string[]; log: string }`, `export interface TransactionRound { round: number; reds: RoundRed[] }` in src/runloop/types.ts). A value thrown (an answer write, the interrupt, the hook): before the first commit → before restored and every card {status "skipped", reason "fault", attempts 0, winningVariant null, acceptanceLog "", earlierFailures [], commit null, diffstat null}; after → the committed keep "written", the rest that outcome, nothing restored; fault = the Error's message. The Run Report: runId, completedAt deps.now(), branch, processor deps.config.id, generations W's, outcomes in deck order, usageTotals W's plus every retry request's (cost null when none), requests W's rows then the retries' in send order, then rounds, stop and fault, each when set (fault the last key). deps.onVariant sees every request (W's verdicts are those of the "true" acceptance).

